  "book_code": "GEN",
  "chapter": 12,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the LORD had said to Abram, Depart from thy country, and from thy kindred, and from thy father's house, to a land that I will show thee:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will make of thee a great nation, and I will bless thee, and make thy name great; and thou shalt be a blessing:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will bless them that bless thee, and curse him that curseth thee: and in thee shall all families of the earth be blessed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So Abram departed, as the LORD had spoken to him, and Lot went with him: and Abram ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seventy and five years old when he departed from Haran.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abram took Sarai his wife, and Lot his brother's son, and all their substance that they had gathered, and the souls that they had gotten in Haran; and they went to go forth into the land of Canaan; and into the land of Canaan they came.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abram passed through the land to the place of Sichem, to the plain of Moreh. And the Canaanite ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " then in the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD appeared to Abram, and said, To thy seed will I give this land: and there he erected an altar to the LORD, who appeared to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he removed from thence to a mountain on the east of Beth-el, and pitched his tent, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "having",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Beth-el on the west, and Hai on the east: and there he erected an altar to the LORD, and called upon the name of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abram journeyed, going on still towards the south.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there was a famine in the land: and Abram went down into Egypt to dwell there; for the famine ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " grievous in the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, when he had come near to enter into Egypt, that he said to Sarai his wife, Behold now, I know that thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a fair woman to look upon:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore it will come to pass, when the Egyptians shall see thee, that they will say, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his wife: and they will kill me, but they will save thee alive.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Say, I pray thee, thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my sister: that it may be well with me for thy sake; and my soul shall live because of thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, that when Abram had come into Egypt, the Egyptians beheld the woman that she ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " very fair.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The princes also of Pharaoh saw her, and commended her before Pharaoh: and the woman was taken into Pharaoh's house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he treated Abram well for her sake: and he had sheep, and oxen, and he-asses, and men-servants, and maid-servants, and she-asses, and camels.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the LORD afflicted Pharaoh and his house with great plagues, because of Sarai, Abram's wife.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pharaoh called Abram, and said, What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast done to me? why didst thou not tell me that she ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy wife?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why saidst thou, She ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my sister? so I might have taken her to me for a wife: now therefore behold thy wife, take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and go thy way.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GEN.12.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:GEN.12.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pharaoh commanded ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " men concerning him: and they sent him away, and his wife, and all that he had.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
